ted (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>", "他修好了吗", "HELP其实可以改个名字把,叫outbox把是不是更合适,让codex可以在阶段性成果的时候汇报一下,你来检查一下,我发现很多次跑完了,发现有问题白跑了,要及时发现问题,及时止损,建立这样一种机制", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>bfwvbxwoj</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XrEhEgarvBj4KRnp3eqLNH</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-agent-eval/e0bc569c-1378-4d2b-acc8-68aea273a8b3/tasks/bfwvbxwoj.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"cd ~/.claude/refs &amp;&amp; python3 - &lt;&lt;'E'\np='delegation-tools.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"No HELP.md, nothing finished. State in the prompt the only allowed ways to\\n  end the turn (committed + report, or HELP.md / BUDGET-QUESTION.md written), and check for\",\n            \"No outbox entry, nothing finished. State in the prompt the only allowed ways to\\n  end the turn (committed + report, or an OUTBOX [BLOCKED] entry / BUDGET-QUESTION.md written), and check for\")\ns=s.replace(\"- **Delegates pre-create empty `HELP.md` / `INBOX.md`.** A watcher that fires on file existence\\n  false-alarms at minute 0. Say \\\"create HELP.md only if there is a problem\\\" and make the\",\n            \"- **Delegates pre-create empty `OUTBOX.md` / `INBOX.md` (and used to with `HELP.md`).** A watcher that fires on file existence\\n  false-alarms at minute 0. Say \\\"create OUTBOX.md only when you write an entry\\\" and make the\")\nadd='''- **Outbox protocol: staged gates so a wrong premise dies cheap (2026-10-14).** Several runs\n  finished only to show the premise was wrong (wrong client class, missing `entity_types`,\n  tests that could not fail) and the whole cost was lost. Mechanism, all in the repo of tools:\n  `~/.claude/bin/codex-watch.sh &lt;pid&gt; &lt;sid&gt; &lt;outdir&gt; [hb] [stall]` exits on each new\n  `OUTBOX.md` entry (kind = MILESTONE / GATE / BLOCKED), on budget, stall, heartbeat and exit;\n  re-arm after each exit except DONE (it remembers the bytes already reported).\n  `~/.claude/bin/codex-wait-inbox.sh &lt;outdir&gt; [timeout]` blocks the delegate at a gate until\n  `INBOX.md` has content, prints it, archives it as `INBOX.read-N.md`, exits 3 on timeout\n  (re-run; never pass a gate without a reply). The delegate's profile\n  (`~/.codex/delegate.config.toml`, `developer_instructions` item 8) already tells it to report\n  at stage ends and wait at gates; the **spec supplies the stages**.\n  Entry format (append-only):\n  `## &lt;time&gt; [MILESTONE|GATE|BLOCKED] &lt;title&gt;` / `done:` / `evidence: &lt;paths&gt;` / `next:` /\n  (gate only) `need: go / change / stop`.\n  Spec skeleton for any run that costs more than a few minutes:\n  1. **S0 dry check (cheap)** — prove the code path / client / endpoint / config under test is\n     the one meant (one request, a log line, an assertion); entry `[MILESTONE]`, I check the\n     evidence before S1.\n  2. **S1 pilot** — one unit, measured cost and one output sample; entry `[GATE]` with the\n     extrapolated total; I check the sample for sanity (right shape, non-empty, plausible\n     numbers) before the fan-out.\n  3. **S2 fan-out** — runs on after my go; `[MILESTONE]` every N units or ~25 min with counts\n     and a sample, so a bad batch is caught after N units, not at the end.\n  4. **S3 finish** — report; `[GATE]` before any commit or other irreversible step.\n  For each gate the spec says what I will look at. In my reply (INBOX) I write go / change /\n  stop and why. Cost of a gate is a wait, which is cheap with the long-wait recipe; the cost\n  it avoids is an entire run.\n'''\nanchor=\"\\n## `dsh`\"\ns=s.replace(anchor, add+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncd ~/.codex &amp;&amp; cp AGENTS.md AGENTS.md.bak-20261014 &amp;&amp; python3 - &lt;&lt;'E'\np='/Users/youxun/.codex/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n- A task spec may mark a gate: write the outbox entry, then run\n  `~/.claude/bin/codex-wait-inbox.sh &lt;outdir&gt;` with the same long-wait pattern and do nothing\n  else until it prints the reply (exit 3 = timeout: run it again, do not proceed).\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ntail -6 AGENTS.md; cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-agent-eval/e0bc569c-1378-4d2b-acc8-68aea273a8b3/scratchpad/cx &amp;&amp; codex exec -p delegate --skip-git-repo-check --cd . \"reply with exactly OK\" &lt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep -E \"^(model|OK|error)\" | head -3\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>", "还没有好吗啊,你的巡检任务好像停了啊", "按你的说的来把"]
